@startuml password_update
title Password Reset - UML Sequence Diagram

hide footbox

actor Client
participant "Tutoring.Api" as Api
participant RequestPasswordResetHandler
participant ResetPasswordHandler
database "SQL Server" as Database
participant OutboxProcessor
queue RabbitMQ
participant EmailConsumer
participant EmailEventDispatcher
participant SmtpMailer
participant "SMTP / Mailpit" as Smtp

Client -> Api : POST /api/auth/password-reset/request\n(email)
Api -> RequestPasswordResetHandler : MediatR command
RequestPasswordResetHandler -> Database : Find account by email
alt account unknown or inactive
    RequestPasswordResetHandler --> Api : no-op (same response either way)
else account active
    RequestPasswordResetHandler -> Database : Invalidate other active reset tokens,\nsave new token hash and outbox event
end
Api --> Client : 204 No Content

OutboxProcessor -> Database : Read unprocessed outbox event
OutboxProcessor -> RabbitMQ : Publish PasswordResetRequested event\n(includes raw reset token)
RabbitMQ -> EmailConsumer : Deliver email event
EmailConsumer -> EmailEventDispatcher : Dispatch PasswordResetRequested
EmailEventDispatcher -> SmtpMailer : Send reset-link email
SmtpMailer -> Smtp : Send email
Smtp --> Client : Reset link

Client -> Api : POST /api/auth/password-reset\n(token, new password)
Api -> ResetPasswordHandler : MediatR command
ResetPasswordHandler -> Database : Find token by hash; validate\nunused, not invalidated, unexpired

alt invalid token
    ResetPasswordHandler --> Api : InvalidPasswordResetTokenException
    Api --> Client : 401 ProblemDetails
else valid token
    ResetPasswordHandler -> ResetPasswordHandler : Validate password policy
    ResetPasswordHandler -> Database : ChangePassword(), mark token used,\nrevoke all active refresh tokens,\ninvalidate other active reset tokens
    Api --> Client : 204 No Content
end

@enduml
